{
  "requirement": "Every {term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion` type implements\n`trust_but_verify::graph::Criterion<D>` for its\n{term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain`.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    type Ok: Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send;\n\n    fn source_node_id(&self) -> D::NodeId;\n    fn criterion_path(&self) -> CriterionPath;\n    fn version(&self) -> CriterionVersion;\n    fn execute(\n        self,\n        ctx: &mut ValidationContext<'_, D>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Self::Ok, ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the tests adequate for `requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait`.\n\nThe requirement is a trait-shape contract. Every criterion type implements `Criterion<D>` with these members:\n- `type Ok: Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send`\n- `source_node_id`\n- `criterion_path`\n- `version`\n- a `Send` `execute` future that returns `Result<Self::Ok, ValidationError<D::Error>>`\n\nThe trait carries `Send + Sized` bounds.\n\nThe tests exercise this shape in three ways:\n\n- **Compile-time conformance.** The test criteria implement `Criterion<D>` with this exact associated type and these methods. They include `Review<O>` for `Application` in `tests/contracts.rs`, `Review` for `Memory` in `agent/tests.rs` and `graph/validation_tests.rs`, and the SDK `Review` for `ReviewGraph` in `src/authoring/sdk.rs`. They use several `Ok` types: `Assessment<..>`, `String`, `bool`, `()`, `Vec<String>`, `Value`, and `Cell<u32>`. A trait with different method signatures or `Ok` bounds would fail to compile against them.\n- **Accessor values and `execute` results.** In `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested`, the tests check `source_node_id`, `criterion_path` and `version` through the resulting evidence. They check `execute` through `Validator::verify`, which returns the typed output, and they check that the output round-trips through storage as serialized JSON. The SDK test `review_graph_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk` directly asserts `review().source_node_id()`, `review().criterion_path().segments()` and `review().version()`. It also asserts the executed answer and the persisted and reloaded record. `caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly` checks version comparison. `deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent` checks execution of a plain deterministic criterion.\n- **`Send` and `Sync` boundaries.** `validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync` uses a `Cell<u32>` `Ok`, which is `Send` but not `Sync`. It wraps the futures in a `send(..)` helper that requires `Send`. The `Ok` type therefore needs only `Send`, and the `execute` future is `Send`.\n\nI found no behavior in the requirement that lacks a test. The type-level bounds are compile-time contracts, and the implementing test types would break if the trait deviated from them. The `public_api.rs` test is about exports and adds no further coverage here. No acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "56f4b9fe7da0aa15014b3838508c84537c402f91531e0b341d3e3ebb1b623825",
